.TH WERKMEISTER-CLEAN 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-clean \- Remove orphaned volumes and generated files from stopped features
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister clean\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Also clean volumes for currently active features (implies werkmeister down for each)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be cleaned without actually removing anything
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBWhat it does:\fR
.IP 1. 3
Identifies per\-feature Docker volumes (node_modules, build caches) that belong to stopped features
.IP 2. 3
Removes those orphaned volumes
.IP 3. 3
Releases stale slot entries (features with no running containers or compose file)
.PP
With \fB\-\-all\fR, it first stops all active features (equivalent to running \fBwerkmeister down \-\-volumes\fR for each), then cleans everything.
.PP
\fBWhen to use:\fR
.IP \(bu 3
After extended development with many features started and stopped — volumes accumulate
.IP \(bu 3
Before a fresh start: \fBwerkmeister clean \-\-all\fR
.IP \(bu 3
To check what would be cleaned: \fBwerkmeister clean \-\-dry\-run\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
